Subject: [PATCH 2/2] claude: Keep the mail bookmark up with the list
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: tzouurtmlzlmxqxmwzlszxnswyzqkylq

When all of the outbox had been merged into mail, step 1 of
process-email had nothing to rebase, so the bookmark stayed on an old
mail commit. The pass then indexed the old list and missed every
message that arrived since, until someone moved the bookmark by hand.

Point a bookmark that has no pending mail of its own at the list's
tip. This also covers a bookmark that does not exist yet.
---
change-id: tzouurtmlzlmxqxmwzlszxnswyzqkylq

 .claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
index d29e701..f51a0f0 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
@@ -79,13 +79,18 @@ was accepted, then index the list together with your own pending mail
 so messages you already answered count as replied:
 
     cd ~/lab/mail.jj
-    if [ -z "$(jj log -r "bookmarks(exact:${me})" --no-graph -T 'commit_id')" ]; then
-        jj bookmark create "${me}" -r mail@upstream
+    if [ -z "$(jj log -r "bookmarks(exact:${me}) ~ ::mail@upstream" \
+            --no-graph -T 'commit_id')" ]; then
+        jj bookmark set "${me}" -r mail@upstream
     fi
     jj rebase -b "${me}" -d mail@upstream --skip-emptied
     jj new "${me}"
     notmuch new
 
+A bookmark with no pending mail, missing or merged in full, is
+pointed at the list's tip first. It has nothing to rebase, so the
+rebase alone would leave it behind on an old list.
+
 ## 2. Pick the oldest inbox message
 
     id="$(notmuch search --sort=oldest-first --output=messages \
